{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast!_Just_4_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast! Just 4 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Pythagorean_Theorem_and_Volume_of_Pyramid)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Pythagorean Theorem and Volume of Pyramid)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a rectangle and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbe20733d24579adb2707e9dc19f5c01568a351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DM}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> be a segment perpendicular to the plane of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbe20733d24579adb2707e9dc19f5c01568a351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DM}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> has integer length, and the lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b790cd7e534dde7dfd1e0ab8708c7f80c63cb50e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MA},\\overline{MC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e1067e157113377bc8b04c4f96d0eb3caa0f7464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MB}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> are consecutive odd positive integers (in this order). What is the volume of pyramid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b102937e28583fb3eb313ef5a4eae2a6b7a72c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MABCD?$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/237babaa44af634b687e4fcff85d584d40b30ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }24\\sqrt5 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }60 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }28\\sqrt5\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }66 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }8\\sqrt{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"472\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc298534231e615462c23c9b2d563dc7e5726b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255cb7d077ce80eebe8b3f33d69837d1e6a8f78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD=d.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f42ac43386308064bb6ee2617229af815f5220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC=a+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3ca71cab1894044079b34337984504a720a7d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB=a+4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>As shown below, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26dffdaf7146800f04cef35e039a6e984fcb162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb3fc3869e0de5c347520d1596fe011cfb42b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MBC$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> are both right triangles.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f73763c4c24a6da41ac2ad657eaeef36466d15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300); import graph3; import solids;  currentprojection=orthographic((0.5,-0.25,-0.5)); triple A, B, C, D, M; A = (-2sqrt(10),0,0); B = (-2sqrt(10),-6sqrt(2),0); C = (0,-6sqrt(2),0); D = (0,0,0); M = (0,0,3); draw(surface(M--A--D--cycle),yellow); draw(surface(M--B--C--cycle),yellow); draw(D--A--B--C^^A--M^^B--M^^C--M^^D--M); draw(C--D,dashed); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^M,linewidth(4.5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,2*dir(A-B)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,2*dir(B-A)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,2*dir(C-D)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,2*dir(D-C)); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,2*dir((1,1,0))); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,midpoint(M--A),2*dir((-1,-1,0)),red); label(&quot;$d$&quot;,midpoint(M--D),2*dir((1,1,0)),red); label(&quot;$a+2$&quot;,midpoint(M--C),2*dir((1,-1,0)),red); label(&quot;$a+4$&quot;,midpoint(M--B),2*dir((-1,1,0)),red); [/asy]\" width=\"488\" height=\"292\" />\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b968981b68fe2bd10356f37f2ff7e65405cd44c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{6} AD^2 &amp;= MA^2 - MD^2 &amp;&amp;= a^2 - d^2, \\\\ BC^2 &amp;= MB^2 - MC^2 &amp;&amp;= (a+4)^2 - (a+2)^2. \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"341\" height=\"47\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314bfa1fb251cfe31dbff4a462217c7e4ebce5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=BC$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> in rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/42501e1c7100f340da9bd452bf942219ac6b131b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> we equate the expressions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/161b162afcb4f7b6a3447e0dc08b3813bdfa113f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^2$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a2030d3443c094b8eb430c7c16b829498fd30d23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> then rearrange and factor:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e079414d242e5e0a21622b27d9be7ecf88d8ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2 - d^2 &amp;= (a+4)^2 - (a+2)^2 \\\\ a^2 - d^2 &amp;= 4a + 12 \\\\ a^2 - 4a - d^2 &amp;= 12 \\\\ (a-2)^2 - d^2 &amp;= 16 \\\\ (a+d-2)(a-d-2) &amp;= 16. \\end{align*}\" width=\"342\" height=\"128\" />\nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f263792fc64acc05e0e47d5de6c0230e2bb27c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4aea7ff3de9a1dc8763e65f1090b46b7c2772a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-d-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> have the same parity, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6834cc4e36753770d091cee5c17f63debda127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d-2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598d561b2df9b1b310cf4a8f568bf4d1df999a5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-d-2=2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/4946bf7790fc2f082582d337bdfc861da69bf139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,d)=(7,3).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Applying the Pythagorean Theorem to right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26dffdaf7146800f04cef35e039a6e984fcb162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155fede0237cbcae9cb567591fea7cce1bca8e07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MCD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbc265e277af12c2104cfe2885a22265840d2cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=2\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a35e2b91e37b504c33512defcfb11b10f74eb425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=6\\sqrt2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"23\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Let the brackets denote areas. Together, the volume of pyramid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/46473945f3d28b9b1df6ba93795c6c2d261331eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MABCD$\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832ad1e5bfe11606c247f00dfbba4c6924300e6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac13\\cdot [ABCD]\\cdot MD = \\frac13\\cdot (AD\\cdot CD)\\cdot MD = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }24\\sqrt5}.\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"37\" />\n~Lopkiloinm ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07daaeb34175de9e89ff0ceb2668cfd950c92814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=b$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/353b86bbdedcf9e4abc7b7d6552d94451bb9bfb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=a$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31fb34078ad18b2f0e65d3ee7e485ee89effc38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD=x$\" width=\"69\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311d9149f8fcb7ef2f20223e104f83f911027753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC=t$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369a91546611abc61b81d302dd8cbfd6ce085774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA=t-2$\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e4651fb38d93b28d65b065fd9d9a1995880e11ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB=t+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We have three equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cefd238910d1fadeedc5037da5f209c9ac81ed1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2 + x^2 &amp;= t^2, \\\\ a^2 + b^2 + x^2 &amp;= t^2 + 4t + 4, \\\\ b^2 + x^2 &amp;= t^2 - 4t + 4. \\end{align*}\" width=\"205\" height=\"72\" />\nSubstituting the first and third equations into the second equation, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee268bdfef57a2e4b50e31e5d2d4aa70ca7a4e0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} t^2 - 8t - x^2 &amp;= 0 \\\\ (t-4)^2 - x^2 &amp;= 16 \\\\ (t-4-x)(t-4+x) &amp;= 16. \\end{align*}\" width=\"213\" height=\"72\" />\nTherefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262741ba3c6ae57bba79c9427d258c845171f01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 9$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Solving for other values, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c18f8bf71b0abaa250fe1d11088ccdac7758dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f85056b89441a8cbc778845246eb90c7cf22d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"21\" />.\nThe volume is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2badfefaede7b4172e5372d64ef282b4bb4ec17c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{3} abx = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }24\\sqrt5}.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>~jamess2022 (burntTacos)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First and foremost, the diagram must be drawn.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8de7bc260f2ef2ab14ac141efb964d5a857fee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(250);  pair A = (0,0); pair B = (4.5,0); pair C = (6,1.1); pair D = (1.5,1.1); pair M = (1.5,3.45);  draw(A--B); draw(C--B); draw(A--D, dashed); draw(C--D, dashed); draw(M--A); draw(M--B); draw(M--C); draw(M--D, dashed);  draw((1.5,1.3)--(1.7,1.3)--(1.7,1.1));  dot(A,linewidth(4.5)); dot(B,linewidth(4.5)); dot(C,linewidth(4.5)); dot(D,linewidth(4.5)); dot(M,linewidth(4.5));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, N);  label(&quot;$x$&quot;, midpoint(M--A), NW, red); label(&quot;$x+4$&quot;, midpoint(M--B), SE, red); label(&quot;$x+2$&quot;, midpoint(M--C), NE, red); label(&quot;$a$&quot;, midpoint(A--D), W, red); label(&quot;$b$&quot;, midpoint(A--B), S, red); label(&quot;$I$&quot;, midpoint(M--D), E, red); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"258\" />\nWith the diagram, an impulse to utilize Pythagorean theorem is created. Thereby, the shaded right triangles may be used.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/2241ac14e00b5b115e3bba40ca13ce527508a3c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph;  size(250);  pair A = (0,0); pair B = (4.5,0); pair C = (6,1.1); pair D = (1.5,1.1); pair M = (1.5,3.45);  draw(A--B); draw(C--B); draw(A--D, dashed); draw(C--D, dashed); draw(D--B, dashed); draw(M--A); draw(M--B); draw(M--C); draw(M--D, dashed);  draw(M--A--D--cycle, blue); draw(M--B--D--cycle, green); draw(M--C--D--cycle, red);  draw((1.5,1.3)--(1.7,1.3)--(1.7,1.1));  dot(A,linewidth(4.5)); dot(B,linewidth(4.5)); dot(C,linewidth(4.5)); dot(D,linewidth(4.5)); dot(M,linewidth(4.5));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, N);  label(&quot;$x$&quot;, midpoint(M--A), NW, red); label(&quot;$x+4$&quot;, midpoint(M--B), SE, red); label(&quot;$x+2$&quot;, midpoint(M--C), NE, red); label(&quot;$a$&quot;, midpoint(A--D), W, red); label(&quot;$b$&quot;, midpoint(A--B), S, red); label(&quot;$I$&quot;, midpoint(M--D), E, red); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p>The following equations could be obtained from Pythagorean Theorem.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb41a0b2f7d61b29e22949f589fff3461ccdb4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     I^2+a^2&amp;=x^2 \\\\     I^2+b^2&amp;=(x+2)^2 \\\\     I^2+a^2+b^2&amp;=(x+4)^2 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"179\" height=\"75\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are integers, writing an equation in terms of only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> may be beneficial for trial and error.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f803b3ea3f11da551bb72dd6a716d2ef5fd0046.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     x^2+(x+2)^2&amp;=(x+4)^2+I^2 \\\\     2x^2+4x+4&amp;=x^2+8x+16+I^2 \\\\     x^2-4x-12&amp;=I^2 \\\\     (x-6)(x+2)&amp;=I^2 \\end{align*}\" width=\"272\" height=\"103\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7f6230166a491e7a471a03829c792496576480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> seems valid since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5ca9c120b168f976115023cc7807ba78aaa755e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I=3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7f6230166a491e7a471a03829c792496576480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7f6230166a491e7a471a03829c792496576480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40decee4f0ea9ad2f79ea51534c07c27c31f22b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1adbc4ed93bbb68db5482feeec84ea0c4fc332c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"21\" />. We could double check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/0445753293bf3e6cfd48b9fa83abca42bbc56bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40+72+9=11^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. Thereby,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdcec89d7d316a6fbb72d26383150993fcd267e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a\\cdot b\\cdot I}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}\\cdot6\\sqrt{2}\\cdot3}{3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }24\\sqrt5}.\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~MaPhyCom\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast.21_Just_4_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast!_Just_4_min!)\">Video Solution (Fast! Just 4 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast! Just 4 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Bo2EvRZdRnA\">https://youtu.be/Bo2EvRZdRnA</a>\n</p><p>~<i>Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4iCAZRUESs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4iCAZRUESs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Pythagorean_Theorem_and_Volume_of_Pyramid.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Pythagorean_Theorem_and_Volume_of_Pyramid)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Pythagorean Theorem and Volume of Pyramid)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Pythagorean Theorem and Volume of Pyramid)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4_Oqp_ECLRw\">https://youtu.be/4_Oqp_ECLRw</a>\n</p><p>~pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B\">2021 AMC 12B</a></b> 